{
  "case_id": "2012-12-43",
  "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case has its origins in a decision by the British government in the Major Thatcher years to privatize a number of previously State-owned utilities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 12-43, PPL Corporation and Subsidiaries v. the Commissioner of Internal Revenue. Mr. Clement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: See, I have a problem with this argument because it assumes a way of looking at this, but it's an assumption. You can look at it in either way. You can look at it as they made too much money, we want a part of that profit, or they paid too little for what they got."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose everyone in the case conceded that the purpose of this statute was to compensate the government for having valued the shares at too low a price, and this was stated right in the enactment. Would that change your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "concedes that this tax operates exactly like a 51.75 percent tax on profits above a threshold, a threshold of 4/9ths of the floatation value."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor's amicus brief",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As the professor's amicus brief points out, if you reformulated this into an average annual profit or left the P over 4 as it was and then divided everything else by 9, this would become a 207 percent tax on --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think an important point here is that the Petitioners have conceded that if Parliament had chosen a different valuation method, like the stock price, for any particular company and then subtracted out the floatation value, that that would not be a tax on income, that that would be a value tax."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: On that -- on the question of how to treat, I -- there isn't authority, but, I mean, if I'm quite honest about how I think about it, I think the people in the tax court actually, usually, know more about it than the judges who are not on the tax court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I thought you would -- you would answer that, that the Commissioner gets some credit, too."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. O'CONNELL: I think that would not be an income tax because they are using a valuation formula that is imputing a value on the company and then taxing that value."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. O'Connell -- if the Court should go the way the Fifth Circuit went -- the way the Tax Court went -- could the regulation be changed so it wouldn't happen again?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2012-12-43",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3f5cf18a023d3c03338abed4b6ac1e9319d2ecbf58625fe57c5d644c0ca641a4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3f5cf18a023d-0002-0011",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:14 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
